  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 125 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nMonday night we continue our warming trend as broad ridging over \nSouth Central Texas becomes more amplified heading into the late \nweek period. Each day we will continue to warm until we eventually \njump back above normal for highs beginning Tuesday and especially\nWednesday and into the weekend. This means we should see highs in\nthe low 80s before highs ramp up into the upper 80s to low 90 by \nthe end of the week. Additionally we will see the return of more \nhumid conditions then what we currently have this weekend with \ndewpoints back into the 50s and 60s compared to the very dry 30s \nand 40s currently. Eventually, a trough is progged to move over \nthe western U.S late in the period but the elongated upper ridge \nmay limit impacts for our area associated with this feature. At \nthe moment the forecast looks to remain dry and continues to be \nthat way throughout the entire extended portion of the forecast.",
